decisions:
  - id: TD-2026-10-24-447
    decision: 8.0.1 ships with loops disabled; Phase 0 is the orchestration closure point
    rationale: The signed app bundles no paradigm CLI, so builtin loop checks fail; testers get the Mac build sooner.
learnings:
  - Gate on the compiled release define, never a user file or the log; the env override must be ignored in release builds.
  - Add a release-script assertion that the staged kernel is a release build, since a dev dist wrapped into the app would ship loops on.
  - 'Counts and lists must filter from one source: hiding a card in the stack but counting it elsewhere leaves a number with nothing behind it.'
  - turn.economy rows need a per-call context series and the conductor model, or the Phase 1 metrics cannot be computed from them.
  - Local packages/gnomon/dist is a release build on the founder's machine, which makes release-pins, gate-gnomon-publish, version and daemon-lifecycle tests fail until the next release build.
verification:
  status: partial
  details:
    note: Targeted tests pass in all three packages; full gnomon suite has 11 failures that read the local release dist or stale dist version; not proven on a clean checkout.
